##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# GitHub #210: a static micropolygon's extra output (an AOV, here the surface variable s) is interpolated
# bilinearly between all four corners under the default "smooth" interpolation. The patch spans the image:
# 64 pixels wide, ShadingRate 16 dices it into micropolygons 4 pixels wide. The test reads a row near the top
# of its micropolygons, where the v3 corner weighs most (with v2 read in its place the row is plateaus).
version 3.03
Hider "reyes"
Option "shaderformat" "default" ["rslo"]
PixelSamples 1 1
PixelFilter "box" 1 1
Quantize "rgba" 0 0 0 0
Display "shading-interpolation-aov-smooth-reyes-rgba.tif" "file" "rgba"
Display "+shading-interpolation-aov-smooth-reyes.tif" "file" "varying float s"
Projection "orthographic"
ScreenWindow 0 1 0 1
Format 64 64 1
Clipping 0.1 100
Translate 0 0 1
WorldBegin
  ShadingRate 16
  Surface "show_st"
  Patch "bilinear" "P" [0 0 0  1 0 0  0 1 0  1 1 0]
WorldEnd
